<title>JAPAN: Japan December soybean imports rise 3.9 pct yr/yr.</title>
<headline>Japan December soybean imports rise 3.9 pct yr/yr.</headline>
<dateline>TOKYO 1997-02-24</dateline>
<text>
<p>Japan's soybean imports in December totalled 490,600 tonnes, up 3.9 percent on the same month a year earlier, Finance Ministry data released on Monday showed.</p>
<p>Total imports throughout calendar 1996 reached 4.87 million tonnes against 4.81 million tonnes a year earlier.</p>
<p>The breakdown was as follows (in tonnes):</p>
<p>			 Dec 96     Nov 96	Dec 95</p>
<p> Total imports     490,600    252,599     472,175</p>
<p>Major suppliers of soybeans (in tonnes):  U.S.		  405,780    213,866     431,003</p>
<p> Bolivia		 9,283     16,354	  ----</p>
<p> Paraguay	     46,494     12,255	 7,190</p>
<p>-- Tokyo Commodities Desk +81-3-3432-7391</p>
</text>
